		{
			"id": "115092160299047208",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://vickerson.me/@josh/115092160289307888",
			"author": {
				"name": "Josh “Yoshi” Vickerson",
				"url": "https://vickerson.me/@josh",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/017/460/209/559/248/original/19901369730a3977.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-08-26T00:09:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> A client of mine had his Wordpress site hacked because of plugins. Hackers published a lot of… unsavory content to his site.</p><p>Made pitching moving to Eleventy very easy 🤷‍♂️</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115092293499459193",
			"parentId": "115091525384850289",
			"url": "https://social.vivaldi.net/@jadonn/115092293446709443",
			"author": {
				"name": "jadonn",
				"url": "https://social.vivaldi.net/@jadonn",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/960/025/939/613/912/original/f2a89eefd5025cbe.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-08-26T00:43:48.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I wonder if they've fallen prey to their own experience of running WordPress as a hosting provider. I used to work in technical support for a WordPress-focused web host, and restoring hacked or messed up sites was a very common thing we had to do. However, I would expect each individual user maybe only had to do a full site restore once or twice in the lifetime of their WordPress websites.</p><p>From the host's perspective, WordPress site recovery is essential because you see all the sites getting hacked all the time, and this becomes a really attractive feature.</p><p>I would always try to remind myself (even still today in customer service settings as a customer) that I am the only person the folks on the other end of the line might talk to today, even though I might have talked to 40-50 people in a given day, and so the experience of the interaction is very different for them than for me</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
